WEBVTT

00:00.350 --> 00:08.020
A group policy may begin at headquarters, but it has to remain defensible
across jurisdictions, legal entities and lines of business.

00:08.020 --> 00:15.689
Before a policy is approved, a control is attested or an assurance opinion is
formed, reviewers need the governing source, the

00:15.689 --> 00:19.341
applicable wording and a clear record of what was checked.

00:19.341 --> 00:25.185
When that evidence is fragmented across a multinational document estate,
documentary uncertainty becomes operational and regulatory

00:25.185 --> 00:25.550
risk.

00:26.550 --> 00:29.907
A large bank does not work from one document.

00:29.907 --> 00:35.503
Group policy connects to local addenda, procedures, control descriptions,
approved exceptions, change records and external

00:35.503 --> 00:35.876
requirements.

00:35.876 --> 00:41.844
The same policy family may apply differently by country, regulator, legal
entity, product or effective date.

00:41.844 --> 00:45.202
A local requirement can add to the group minimum.

00:45.202 --> 00:48.186
An exception can change the route to approval.

00:48.186 --> 00:54.154
A cited source can be replaced while the policy that depends on it remains in
circulation.

00:54.154 --> 00:57.139
The review problem is not simply finding words.

00:57.139 --> 00:59.750
It is establishing the relationships between them.

01:00.750 --> 01:07.793
Cortessa's target banking-site deployment gives each authorised policy,
compliance and assurance reviewer a dedicated, self-sufficient

01:07.793 --> 01:10.141
box inside the site boundary.

01:10.141 --> 01:17.185
Local policies, addenda, procedures, ingestion, index, on-device model and
source viewer remain on that box.

01:17.185 --> 01:21.411
Audit and Ask run locally against the approved corpus.

01:21.411 --> 01:25.167
Author remains in development and requires further testing.

01:25.167 --> 01:33.150
The reviewer controls the local working context and remains responsible for
applicability, interpretation and every approved revision.

01:34.150 --> 01:41.251
Reviewer boxes are designed to connect through group-policy, local-compliance
and independent-assurance departmental nodes to an

01:41.251 --> 01:45.039
on-site hub, entirely inside that site's air-gapped boundary.

01:45.039 --> 01:48.826
Department-default scope and selected cross-department sharing remain
explicit.

01:48.826 --> 01:54.507
This does not claim an international network between bank sites or
jurisdictions.

01:54.507 --> 01:59.242
This is the target architecture, not a deployed production-network claim.

01:59.242 --> 02:05.869
The offline contract and application foundations exist; authenticated
transport, key operations, scheduling, backup, recovery,

02:05.869 --> 02:08.710
assurance and rollout remain deployment work.

02:09.710 --> 02:11.695
Audit leads the Cortessa workflow.

02:11.695 --> 02:18.048
It works across the selected policy corpus rather than waiting for one
question at a time.

02:18.048 --> 02:24.797
It can surface missing sources, revision uncertainty, inconsistent terminology
or an unexplained divergence between group and local

02:24.797 --> 02:25.194
wording.

02:25.194 --> 02:31.150
Each result is a cited documentary question for authorised review, not a
finding of non-compliance.

02:32.150 --> 02:36.550
Each audit candidate leads back to the passage that created it.

02:36.550 --> 02:44.150
The reviewer can inspect the source, surrounding wording, effective date and
local context before deciding whether the discrepancy is

02:44.150 --> 02:44.550
genuine.

02:44.550 --> 02:52.150
Ask supports the same investigation with cited answers from the approved
corpus and can refuse when evidence is absent.

02:52.150 --> 02:53.350
Verified establishes provenance.

02:53.350 --> 02:57.750
It does not establish legal interpretation, policy correctness or
jurisdictional applicability.

02:58.750 --> 03:03.001
A multinational bank cannot outsource local interpretation to a language
model.

03:03.001 --> 03:08.025
The relevant legal entity, jurisdiction, regulator, policy state and effective
date all matter.

03:08.025 --> 03:15.753
Local compliance and legal specialists determine what applies, how an apparent
conflict should be resolved, and whether an exception is

03:15.753 --> 03:16.140
valid.

03:16.140 --> 03:19.231
Cortessa makes the evidence route and uncertainty visible.

03:19.231 --> 03:21.550
The authorised specialist makes the judgement.

03:22.550 --> 03:27.686
The first line owns the business activity, its controls and its operational
evidence.

03:27.686 --> 03:32.822
The second line sets the framework, oversees risk and challenges
interpretation or implementation.

03:32.822 --> 03:36.773
The third line independently assesses the framework and the evidence.

03:36.773 --> 03:42.699
Cortessa can support source investigation and traceability for each line,
while preserving their separate responsibilities.

03:42.699 --> 03:48.230
It does not become the control owner, the compliance authority or the internal
auditor.

03:49.230 --> 03:56.365
A reviewer-approved revision can carry signed identity, content hash, parent
lineage and approved audit context through its

03:56.365 --> 03:59.723
departmental node and, where authorised, the on-site hub.

03:59.723 --> 04:02.661
Conflicting branches and missing ancestry remain explicit.

04:02.661 --> 04:08.537
The hub cannot approve an exception, attest a control or choose the governing
interpretation.

04:08.537 --> 04:12.315
Receipt does not certify or automatically index a document.

04:12.315 --> 04:15.253
The receiving reviewer governs import and use.

04:15.253 --> 04:19.870
The local Ledger supports inspection without replacing the bank's approval
record.

04:20.870 --> 04:26.442
The right first engagement is a bounded paid evaluation, not a theatre
demonstration.

04:26.442 --> 04:29.871
Compare matched tasks against the bank's current workflow.

04:29.871 --> 04:37.587
Measure the time to locate and inspect the governing source, reviewer effort,
accepted and rejected findings, false-finding burden,

04:37.587 --> 04:40.159
unanswered questions, traceability and evidence-package completeness.

04:40.159 --> 04:43.588
Include difficult documents, conflicting wording and absent sources.

04:43.588 --> 04:48.303
Record corpus preparation and setup effort as part of the result.

04:48.303 --> 04:55.590
The evaluation should show where Cortessa helps, where it fails and what must
change before any expansion.

04:56.590 --> 04:59.167
Observed failures become bounded development work.

04:59.167 --> 05:06.897
Retrieval gaps, document handling, access requirements and workflow friction
are remediated and retested against the agreed task set.

05:06.897 --> 05:15.487
The outcome is evidence for the next decision: whether the workflow and one
departmental exchange merit further hardening, a wider

05:15.487 --> 05:18.493
corpus or controlled expansion at that site.

05:18.493 --> 05:25.365
Cortessa claims no bank deployment, completed site rollout, regulator
approval, complete obligation mapping or guaranteed saving.

05:25.365 --> 05:29.230
The architecture must be demonstrated in the customer's environment.

05:30.230 --> 05:31.973
Bring one policy family.

05:31.973 --> 05:35.459
Select the jurisdictions represented in the local corpus.

05:35.459 --> 05:38.510
Agree the evidence standard and authorised reviewers.

05:38.510 --> 05:42.432
Test local evidence work and one governed departmental exchange.

05:42.432 --> 05:46.790
Start a conversation about a scoped global-banking evaluation with Cortessa.
